{{wikipedia|lang=ms}}

===Etymology===
{{compound|ms|putra|gloss1=prince|jaya|gloss2=success}}, ultimately from {{der|ms|sa|पुत्र}} + {{m|sa|जय|tr=jayá}}; from the name of the first Prime Minister of Malaysia, Tunku Abdul Rahman Putra.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|ms|/putərad͡ʒaja/|a=Johor-Selangor}}
*:<small>Note: Unlike many other Malay words that end with an "a", the final-syllable "a" in "putra" and "jaya" in "Putrajaya" are not reduced to a schwa.</small>
* {{IPA|ms|/putərad͡ʒaja/|a=Riau-Lingga}}
* {{rhymes|ms|ajə|jə|ə}}
